Package: noqtis
Type: Package
Title: Notary of Quantum-Safe Traceable Inputs and Seals
Version: 0.2.2
Authors@R: c(
    person(c("Vansh", "Singh"), "Ruhela", email = "vsruhela@proton.me",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-1750-3592", GitHub = "rootcoder007")))
Description: A post-quantum cryptography toolkit built on the dependency-free
    'NOQTIS' C library. Generate key pairs, then sign and verify with
    lattice-based 'ML-DSA', hash-based 'SLH-DSA', 'Ed25519' or hybrid
    'ML-DSA'+'Ed25519' signatures that need both halves to verify; establish
    shared secrets with 'ML-KEM' or 'HQC' key encapsulation, and seal a
    message or a file to an 'ML-KEM' key; hash with 'SHA-2', 'SHA-3', 'SHAKE'
    or 'BLAKE2b', with 'HMAC', and keep secret keys under a passphrase with
    'Argon2id'. A whole directory can be sealed under one signature and later
    verified offline; a 'Merkle' proof shows chosen files to someone without
    revealing the others, and signed statements rotate or revoke a sealing
    key. Tables can be pinned to a schema and to summaries that show later
    drift, and results wrapped in 'DSSE' envelopes. Keys and 'nonces' come
    from the operating system's random generator, not from the one in R.
